menu "V2X FCE"

config MCUX_COMPONENT_component.v2x_fce
    bool "v2x_fce"
    select MCUX_COMPONENT_driver.mu1
    help
      EdgeLock V2X / FCE (Fast Crypto Engine) firmware service driver. Sibling
      of ele_crypto and v2x_crypto: drives the FCE service (an LTC-AES core
      coupled with an AHB-DMA engine on the V2X enclave) over its dedicated
      message unit using the generic MU hardware driver (fsl_mu) and enclave
      message framing, but with the PRIME / FCE command opcodes and payloads (see the
      EdgeLock Secure Enclave User Guide). Provides AES-GCM authenticated

      encrypt/decrypt with plain AES/HMAC key loading.

config V2X_FCE_DDR_SCRATCH_BASE
    hex "V2X FCE DDR scratch buffer base address"
    default 0x86000000
    depends on MCUX_COMPONENT_component.v2x_fce
    help
      No prefix in generated macro
      Physical base address of the plain DDR scratch region the FCE AHB-DMA
      engine uses to stage the AES-GCM Status / TAG / Input / Output / AAD
      buffers. The FCE addresses this region directly with the same physical
      address the masters use, so it must point at a DDR range reserved for the
      application (default 0x86000000, i.e. the 0x86000000-0x89FFFFFF window on
      the i.MX943 EVK).

endmenu
